  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Customers also differ in how they buy. Store purchases are usually the highest, while catalog purchases are lower. Web visits are common, but visiting the website does not always mean the customer actually buys something."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Relationships Between Customer Characteristics\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 700x500 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "plt.figure(figsize=(7, 5))\n",
    "sns.scatterplot(data=df, x=\"Income\", y=\"TotalSpending\", alpha=0.5)\n",
    "plt.title(\"Income vs Total Spending\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Income\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Total Spending\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Customers with higher income seem to spend more in general. So income and spending are related, but they are still not exactly the same variable."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 19,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1200x500 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.scatterplot(data=df, x=\"Age\", y=\"TotalSpending\", alpha=0.5, ax=axes[0])\n",
    "axes[0].set_title(\"Age vs Total Spending\")\n",
    "axes[0].set_xlabel(\"Age\")\n",
    "axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Total Spending\")\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.scatterplot(data=df, x=\"Recency\", y=\"TotalSpending\", alpha=0.5, ax=axes[1])\n",
    "axes[1].set_title(\"Recency vs Total Spending\")\n",
    "axes[1].set_xlabel(\"Recency\")\n",
    "axes[1].set_ylabel(\"Total Spending\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Age does not look as strongly connected to total spending as income does. Recency also does not show a very clear pattern with spending, but it is still useful because it tells us how long it has been since the customer last bought something."
   ]
  },
